entic Workflows Documentation](https://github.com/github/gh-aw)\n\n\n\n\u0026gt; [!TIP]\n\u0026gt; To configure threat detection behavior, update the frontmatter:\n\u0026gt; ```yaml\n\u0026gt; safe-outputs:\n\u0026gt;   threat-detection:\n\u0026gt;     continue-on-error: true   # Warnings only (default)\n\u0026gt;     # continue-on-error: false  # Strict mode — block safe outputs\n\u0026gt; ```\n\n---\n\n\u0026gt; This issue is automatically managed by GitHub Agentic Workflows. Do not close this issue manually.\n\u0026gt;\n\u0026gt; **No action to take** - Do not assign to an agent.\n\n\n\n\u0026gt; - [x] expires  on Sep 25, 2026, 9:13 AM UTC","comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-26T09:13:49Z","labels":["agentic-workflows"],"number":4,"state":"OPEN","title":"[aw] Detection Runs","updated_at":"2026-08-26T09:13:50Z","user":{"login":"github-actions"}},{"body":"### Workflow Failure\n\n**Workflow:** [Weekly Research](https://github.com/githubnext/agentics/blob/[REDACTED]/workflows/weekly-research.md)  \n**Branch:** main  \n**Run:** https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586\n\n\n\u0026gt; [!WARNING]\n\u0026gt; **Engine Failure**: The `claude` engine terminated unexpectedly.\n\n**Last agent output:**\n```\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.736Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;github\u0026#34;: Cleared connection cache for reconnection\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.736Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;safeoutputs\u0026#34;: HTTP connection closed after 0s (cleanly)\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.737Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;safeoutputs\u0026#34;: Cleared connection cache for reconnection\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.740Z [DEBUG] LSP server manager shut down successfully\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;github\u0026#34;: HTTP connection dropped after 0s uptime\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;github\u0026#34;: Connection error: SSE stream disconnected: AbortError: The operation was aborted.\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;github\u0026#34;: Terminal connection error 1/3\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;safeoutputs\u0026#34;: HTTP connection dropped after 0s uptime\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;safeoutputs\u0026#34;: Connection error: SSE stream disconnected: AbortError: The operation was aborted.\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server \u0026#34;safeoutputs\u0026#34;: Terminal connection error 1/3\n```\n\n\n\n### Action Required\n\n**Assign this issue to an agent** to debug and fix the issue.\n\n\n\nDebug with any coding agent\n\nUse this prompt with any coding agent (GitHub Copilot, Claude, Gemini, etc.):\n\n````\nDebug the agentic workflow failure using https://raw.githubusercontent.com/github/gh-aw/main/debug.md\n\nThe failed workflow run is at https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586\n````\n\n\n\n\nManually invoke the agent\n\nDebug this workflow failure using your favorite Agent CLI and the `agentic-workflows` prompt.\n\n- Start your agent\n- Load the `agentic-workflows` skill from `.github/skills/agentic-workflows/SKILL.md` or \n- Type `debug the agentic workflow weekly-research failure in https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586`\n\n\n\n\u0026gt; [!TIP]\n\u0026gt; \n\u0026gt; Stop reporting this workflow as a failure\n\u0026gt;\n\u0026gt; To stop a workflow from creating failure issues, set `report-failure-as-issue: false` in its frontmatter:\n\u0026gt; ```yaml\n\u0026gt; safe-outputs:\n\u0026gt;   report-failure-as-issue: false\n\u0026gt; ```\n\u0026gt;\n\u0026gt; \n\n\n\u0026gt; Generated from [Weekly Research](https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586) · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Asameerkhansf%2FSameer-Khan+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+weekly-research%22\u0026amp;type=issues)\n\u0026gt; - [x] expires  on Sep 2, 2026, 9:02 AM UTC\n\n\n","created_at":"2026-08-26T09:02:02Z","labels":["agentic-workflows"],"number":3,"state":"OPEN","title":"[aw] Weekly Research failed","updated_at":"2026-08-26T09:02:02Z","user":{"login":"github-actions"}},{"body":"### Workflow Failure\n\n**Workflow:** [Weekly Research](https://github.com/githubnext/agentics/blob/[REDACTED]/workflows/weekly-research.md)  \n**Branch:** main  \n**Run:** https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312\n\n\n\u0026gt; [!WARNING]\n\u0026gt; **Model has no AI credits pricing**: The agent failed because model `openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch` is not in the built-in pricing table and no default fallback pricing is configured. The AWF API proxy rejected every inference request with HTTP 400.\n\nThis is a **configuration issue** — retrying will not help. The model must have pricing before the workflow can run.\n\n\nHow to fix this\n\n**Option 1 — Add pricing in the workflow frontmatter:**\n\n```yaml\nmodels:\n  providers:\n    anthropic:\n      models:\n        \u0026#39;openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch\u0026#39;:\n          cost:\n            # Placeholder values — replace with actual pricing for this model\n            input: \u0026#34;0e0\u0026#34;      # $0.00 per million input tokens\n            output: \u0026#34;0e0\u0026#34;     # $0.00 per million output tokens\n            cache_read: \u0026#34;0e0\u0026#34;  # $0.00 per million cache-read tokens\n            cache_write: \u0026#34;0e0\u0026#34; # $0.00 per million cache-write tokens\n```\n\nUse the provider key matching your engine: `github-copilot` (Copilot), `anthropic` (Claude), `openai` (Codex), or `google` (Gemini). Only `input` and `output` are required; the rest default to zero (or `output` for `reasoning`).\n\n**Option 2 — Map the model to a known model using the `models` field:**\n\nIf `openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch` is an alias for a model already in the built-in pricing table, use the `models` frontmatter field to provide the mapping:\n\n```yaml\nmodels:\n  \u0026#39;openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch\u0026#39;:\n    - claude-sonnet-4-5\n```\n\n**Option 3 — Switch to a model already in the built-in pricing table:**\n\nReplace `openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch` in the workflow frontmatter with a model name that the AWF pricing system recognizes (e.g. `claude-sonnet-4-5`, `gpt-4.1`, `gemini-2.0-flash`).\n\n\n\n\n### Action Required\n\n**Assign this issue to an agent** to debug and fix the issue.\n\n\n\nDebug with any coding agent\n\nUse this prompt with any coding agent (GitHub Copilot, Claude, Gemini, etc.):\n\n````\nDebug the agentic workflow failure using https://raw.githubusercontent.com/github/gh-aw/main/debug.md\n\nThe failed workflow run is at https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312\n````\n\n\n\n\nManually invoke the agent\n\nDebug this workflow failure using your favorite Agent CLI and the `agentic-workflows` prompt.\n\n- Start your agent\n- Load the `agentic-workflows` skill from `.github/skills/agentic-workflows/SKILL.md` or \n- Type `debug the agentic workflow weekly-research failure in https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312`\n\n\n\n\u0026gt; [!TIP]\n\u0026gt; \n\u0026gt; Stop reporting this workflow as a failure\n\u0026gt;\n\u0026gt; To stop a workflow from creating failure issues, set `report-failure-as-issue: false` in its frontmatter:\n\u0026gt; ```yaml\n\u0026gt; safe-outputs:\n\u0026gt;   report-failure-as-issue: false\n\u0026gt; ```\n\u0026gt;\n\u0026gt; \n\n\n\u0026gt; Generated from [Weekly Research](https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312) · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Asameerkhansf%2FSameer-Khan+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+weekly-research%22\u0026amp;type=issues)\n\u0026gt; - [x] expires  on Sep 2, 2026, 8:55 AM UTC\n\n\n","created_at":"2026-08-26T08:55:38Z","labels":["agentic-workflows"],"number":2,"state":"OPEN","title":"[aw] Weekly Research has no AI credits pricing for model (openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch)","updated_at":"2026-08-26T08:55:38Z","user":{"login":"github-actions"}}]
